`sketchCircle()` throws `not implemented` during sketch extrusion

I was building a cylindrical part in `brepjs` to measure its volume before rendering it:

```ts
import opencascade from 'brepjs-opencascade';
import { setOC, sketchCircle, measureVolume } from 'brepjs';
setOC(await opencascade());
const profile = sketchCircle(7);
const body = profile.extrude(12);
console.log(measureVolume(body));
```

This should create a circular sketch, extrude it into a solid, and report its volume. The expected behaviour is described in the API doc comments and `README.md`'s “Quick Start” and “API Styles” sections.

The missing implementations affect both API styles: primitives, disposable shape handles, point/vector conversions, transformations, face and edge queries, extrusion, revolution, sweeps, lofts, volume properties, and cached meshing. Complete the stubs and missing supporting functionality across these files under `src/`:

- `core/`: `definitionMaps.ts`, `disposal.ts`, `errors.ts`, `geometry.ts`, `geometryHelpers.ts`, `occtBoundary.ts`, `result.ts`, `shapeTypes.ts`, `types.ts`, `vecOps.ts`.
- `kernel/`: `meshOps.ts`, `occtAdapter.ts`.
- `measurement/measureFns.ts`.
- `operations/`: `extrudeFns.ts`, `extrudeUtils.ts`, `loftFns.ts`.
- `query/finderFns.ts`.
- `sketching/`: `Sketch.ts`, `cannedSketches.ts`.
- `topology/`: `curveFns.ts`, `faceFns.ts`, `meshCache.ts`, `meshFns.ts`, `shapeFns.ts`, `shapeHelpers.ts`, `shapes.ts`.

